derEscalate hypoxia and tachycardia, reduce blood pressure (improves to 94% on 15L)\nPatient to become increasingly distressed\nIf students commit to intervention – “Have you done this before doctor?”\n\nSim Nurse\nPrompt learner to recognise patient deterioration\nProvide CXR\nIf 2222 not called or alternative help sought – prompt learner that seems to be time critical emergency\nPrepares kit/model for decompression","sourceTrigger":"2222 call put out, repeat A-E assessment underway, commits to decompression, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"ptx-3-0","text":"Recognise deterioration in patient","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"ptx-3-1","text":"Further A-E Assessment","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"ptx-3-2","text":"Call for immediate help: 2222","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"ptx-3-3","text":"Recognises need for immediate needle decompression","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"ptx-3-4","text":"Receives CXR – accurately interprets as tension PTX","objective":"escalation","response":null}]},{"id":"4","name":"SBAR Handover, intervention","observations":{"rr":30,"spo2":84,"hr":135,"sbp":85,"dbp":55,"temp":36.3},"oxygen":"Oxygen at 15 L/min","rhythm":null,"findings":"As above, increasing hypoxia and haemodynamic instability. Periarrest. ","cues":"Sim LeaderTake on role of medical registrar arriving\nReceive SBAR handover and differential\nPrompt for any missed investigations/interpretation\nInitiates/supervises decompression\n\n\nSim Nurse\nReassure patient/acting in background","sourceTrigger":"Completed handover and intervention – scenario end","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"ptx-4-0","text":"Deliver SBAR handover","objective":"handover","response":null},{"id":"ptx-4-1","text":"Offers diagnosis of tension PTX","objective":"handover","response":null},{"id":"ptx-4-2","text":"Completes needle decompression under supervision of medical registrar","objective":"handover","response":null}]}],"investigations":[{"id":"ecg","name":"12-lead ECG","assetPath":null},{"id":"cxr","name":"Chest X-ray","assetPath":null},{"id":"abg","name":"ABG report","assetPath":null}],"review":["Rhythms, timers, transition combinations and treatment responses unset","No diagnostic investigation assets supplied","Original documents preserved in private source archive","Stage 3 faculty cue describes SpO2 improving to 94% on 15 L/min, while stage 4 profile is 84% on 15 L/min. Keep response and timing unset pending faculty review.","No post-decompression recovery profile is supplied. Urgent intervention is not gated by SBAR."],"source":"Original source files: PTX sim checklist.docx, PTx_PatientHx.docx"}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,version) do nothing;
insert into public.scenarios(id,data) values('pe','{"id":"pe","version":1,"title":"Pulmonary embolism","patient":"40-year-old woman","briefing":"Collapse with palpitations and several days of increasing breathlessness.","history":"PATIENT HISTORYScenario 3 – Pulmonary EmbolismRPATIENT HISTORYScenario 3 – Pulmonary EmbolismR\nPATIENT HISTORY\nScenario 3 – Pulmonary Embolism\nR\nPATIENT HISTORY\nScenario 3 – Pulmonary Embolism\nR\n\n\nPresenting Complaint: \n40-year-old female patient\nCollapse with palpitations\n\nHistory of Presenting Complaint\n3-day history of increasingly unwell with intermittent palpitations and feeling out of breath/exercise intolerance\nExperienced sudden light-headedness and collapsed while out shopping this morning\nWitnessed loss of consciousness for ~10-15 seconds\nRapid recovery, no post-ictal confusion\nNo tongue biting, incontinence or seizure activity\n\nRelevant History (if asked) \nReturned from Australia 10 days ago\nTaking combined oral contraceptive pill\nMild pleuritic chest discomfort\n\nPMH \nMigraine\n\nMedications \nCombined oral contraceptive pill\nSumatriptan PRN\n\nAllergies \nNKDA\n\nSocial History \nNon-smoker\nLives with husband\n\n\n\n\n","preparation":"20-minute simulation and 20-minute debrief. Prepare actor/mannequin, monitor and locally reviewed investigation assets. Equipment details need faculty review.","objectives":[{"id":"assessment","text":"Perform a structured history and A-E assessment"},{"id":"interpretation","text":"Interpret investigations and form a differential"},{"id":"escalation","text":"Recognise deterioration and escalate appropriately"},{"id":"handover","text":"Communicate diagnosis and plan using SBAR"}],"stages":[{"id":"1","name":"A-E ASSESSMENT","observations":{"rr":22,"spo2":92,"hr":110,"sbp":120,"dbp":80,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg.  Mildly breathless.","cues":"Sim LeaderProvide history of shortness of breath and collapse\nIf prompted discuss chest pain, travel, OCP\n\nSim Nurse\nAsk for early differential diagnosis \nPrompt learner to consider analgesia","sourceTrigger":"structured A-E completed, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-1-0","text":"Introduce self and confirm patient identity","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-1","text":"Succinct history taking","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-2","text":"A-E Assessment","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-3","text":"Oxygen therapy","objective":"assessment","response":null}]},{"id":"2","name":"Differential Diagnosis/Investigations","observations":{"rr":24,"spo2":90,"hr":122,"sbp":110,"dbp":70,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg. Mildly breathless.","cues":"Sim LeaderPatient to complain of discomfort\nIncreasing hypoxia/tachycardia\n\nSim Nurse\nProvide CXR when asked\nProvide ECG when asked\nProvide ABG when asked\nPrompt learner with patient discomfort\nPrompt learner for anti-emetic if sick\nAsk for most likely diagnosis/differential","sourceTrigger":"Investigations complete/interpretation performed, differential given, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-2-0","text":"Interpretation of ABG","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-1","text":"Interpretation of ECG","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-2","text":"Interpretation of CXR","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-3","text":"Differential diagnosis that includes PE","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-4","text":"Prescribe analgesia/anti-emetic","objective":"interpretation","response":null}]},{"id":"3","name":"Patient Deterioration/Escalation","observations":{"rr":32,"spo2":86,"hr":135,"sbp":85,"dbp":55,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg.  Patient clammy and generally unwell.  Visibly breathless.","cues":"Sim LeaderEscalate hypoxia and tachycardia\nReduce blood pressure\nPatient to become increasingly distressed\n\nSim Nurse\nPrompt learner to recognise patient deterioration\nIf 2222 not called or alternative help sought – prompt learner that seems to be time critical emergency","sourceTrigger":"2222 call put out, repeat A-E assessment underway, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-3-0","text":"Recognise deterioration in patient","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"pe-3-1","text":"Further A-E Assessment","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"pe-3-2","text":"Call for immediate help: 2222","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"pe-3-3","text":"Consider need for anticoagulation","objective":"escalation","response":null},{"id":"pe-3-4","text":"Consider IV fluids","objective":"escalation","response":null}]},{"id":"4","name":"SBAR Handover/Closing","observations":{"rr":32,"spo2":86,"hr":135,"sbp":85,"dbp":55,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg.  Patient clammy and generally unwell.  Visibly breathless.","cues":"Sim LeaderTake on role of medical registrar arriving\nReceive SBAR handover\nPrompt for differential diagnosis\nPrompt for any missed investigations/interpretation\n\n\nSim Nurse\nReassure patient/acting in background","sourceTrigger":"Completed handover – scenario end","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-4-0","text":"Deliver SBAR handover","objective":"handover","response":null},{"id":"pe-4-1","text":"Offer likely diagnosis","objective":"handover","response":null}]}],"investigations":[{"id":"ecg","name":"12-lead ECG","assetPath":null},{"id":"cxr","name":"Chest X-ray","assetPath":null},{"id":"abg","name":"ABG report","assetPath":null}],"review":["Rhythms, timers, transition combinations and treatment responses unset","No diagnostic investigation assets supplied","Original documents preserved in private source archive"],"source":"Original source files: 1-PE_SimChecklist.docx, 5-PE_PatientHx.docx"}'::jsonb) on conflict(id) do nothing;
